<section class="faq-section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>How often should I get a skin cancer screening?</h3>
            <p>We recommend annual screenings for most adults, especially those with risk factors. High-risk individuals may need more frequent exams.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does a biopsy hurt?</h3>
            <p>We use local anesthesia to numb the area, so you shouldn't feel pain during the procedure. You may experience mild soreness afterward.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>What happens if skin cancer is found?</h3>
            <p>We'll discuss the type and stage of the cancer and recommend the most appropriate treatment. Most skin cancers can be successfully treated in our office.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>How can I prevent skin cancer?</h3>
            <p>Use broad-spectrum SPF 30+ sunscreen daily, wear protective clothing, avoid peak sun hours (10am-4pm), and never use tanning beds. Regular skin self-exams are also important.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
